version: "3.0.0"
date-released: "2026-04-12"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.19222021"
abstract: >-
  A systematic framework for quantum algorithm development covering 20 scientific
  problem domains with standardized maturity gates, automated validation, resource
  estimation pipelines, and Azure Quantum integration. Problems are held to explicit
  maturity gates rather than assumed to pass them: 9 problems are at Stage C, 8 remain
  at Stage B, and 3 have reached Stage D, with 20-run calibration ensembles and real
  Azure Quantum Resource Estimator profiles (1.8k to 401k physical qubits). No problem
  currently demonstrates quantum advantage on available hardware, and 11 of the 20 were
  downgraded on I/O bottlenecks or quadratic-only speedups. Implements 10 algorithm
  families (VQE, QAOA, Grover, HHL, Shor, IQAE, swap test, QEC, quantum walk, Trotter
  simulation) using the modern Microsoft QDK (qsharp 1.31.0, no .NET dependency).
  Also includes a deployed evaluation service that routes a natural-language problem
  description to one of five verdicts using a deterministic rule set rather than model
  judgement, a paper classifier measured for over-claim rate against a labelled corpus,
  and generated Q# that is compiled and resource-estimated before it is reported.
  Includes cross-problem comparison dashboard, per-problem detail pages with charts,
  and embedded README documentation.
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - quantum algorithms
  - resource estimation
  - IQAE
  - Q#
  - Azure Quantum
